<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia February palm oil exports 453,287t-SGS.</title>
<headline>Malaysia February palm oil exports 453,287t-SGS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo surveyor Societe Generale de Surveillance (SGS) Malaysia Sdn Bhd said it estimated Malaysia's palm oil exports for February at 453,287 tonnes against 586,046 in January.</p>
<p>It said the exports comprised 178,345 tonnes of RBD palm oil,147,773 tonnes of RBD palm olein and 55,650 tonnes of RBD palm stearin. The other products were 71,519 tonnes.  </p>
<p>Pakistan was the main buyer during the period, taking 88,050 tonnes, followed by Jordan 56,760 tonnes, Japan 38,655 tonnes and China 32,518.</p>
<p>Countries in the European Union bought 62,874 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230-7510)</p>
</text>
